cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Non-MCMC Constraints on the EFC α-Parameter: BAO, Growth-Rate, and Cluster Evidence"
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
type: article
authors:
  - family-names: "Magnusson"
    given-names: "Morten"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0002-4860-5095"
    affiliation: "Symbiose Research, Sandnes, Norway"
date-released: "2026-04-26"
version: "1.0"
license: "CC-BY-4.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/supertedai/EFC"
abstract: >
  We present non-MCMC constraints on the EFC alpha parameter from five
  independent datasets: DESI Y1 BAO, BOSS DR12 BAO, multi-epoch growth
  rate (fσ8), IllustrisTNG cluster statistics, and cosmic chronometer
  H(z). Non-MCMC results are treated strictly as model-comparison
  metrics, not as parameter posteriors. Whereas concurrent MCMC
  inference is degeneracy-limited, cross-validation and likelihood-ratio
  methods yield consistent directional preference for EFC across the
  geometric and growth probes. Non-MCMC results lie within approximately
  0.7 sigma of previously sealed blind predictions, while the MCMC
  posterior shows a 2.8 sigma tension with the same priors. We interpret
  this as methodological tension between inference frameworks under
  degeneracy, not as a detection-level signal.
